⭐ Interview Tip

The expected solution is the Stack approach. Reverse Polish Notation guarantees that whenever an operator appears, its two operands are the most recent values, making a stack the perfect choice. Always pop the operands in the order b first, then a, and compute a op b. This preserves the correct order for non-commutative operations like subtraction and division, resulting in an O(n) time and O(n) space solution.
